# Android wrapper is kept local; this repo publishes the web prototype only
Sukinnect-Android/

# Build output and caches
build/
dist/
node_modules/
.gradle/

# A Python/uv download cache appeared in the working tree on 2026-10-12 — 44 MB of
# _cache/*.job and *.tmp, written by a tool outside this project. Nothing here runs
# Python: the prototype is one HTML file and every instrument in tools/ is Node, so
# this is machine scratch rather than project content. Ignored, not deleted, because
# whatever created it may still expect to find it.
Python/

# Machine-specific and secret local config
local.properties
*.keystore
*.jks
.env

# The business documents are authored sources that sit in this folder for every local AI, and the
# repository is PUBLIC (measured 2026-11-06 with `gh repo view --json visibility`). The Master Plan
# carries a funding ask, a valuation, an investor split, a liquidation waterfall, budget lines and
# named prospective partners; publishing any of that on a public repository is not reversible by
# deleting the file later. So they are ignored rather than committed. Three of them were tracked on
# `feat/mobile-app-visual-pass` and are removed from the index by the commit that adds this block;
# none of them ever reached `origin/main`, so nothing was published. The readable copies under
# `docs/readable/` are ignored for the same reason — they are the same words in another format.
# Owner may reverse this in one line if the repository is made private.
*.docx
docs/readable/

# OS / editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
*.tmp
*.swp

# screenshots written by tools/shot.cjs — looked at, not shipped.
# The pattern is open-ended because the tool is routinely pointed at a fresh
# --out directory to defeat cached image reads, and .shots/ alone let a scratch
# capture into a commit.
.shots*/

# Working copies the instruments write to compare against: a committed blob pulled out
# with `git show` to check a file that is being mutated under it, a mutant fixture a
# falsifier is about to install. Same reasoning as .shots* — they are read, never shipped,
# and a 780 KB duplicate of the app left untracked invites somebody to `git add .` it.
.scratch*/

# Local startup strategy sources contain non-public financial and investor details.
# Keep them on the owner's machine; never commit or publish them.
SUKINNECT_STARTUP_MASTER_PLAN.md
Sukinnect_Master_Plan_*.docx
Sukinnect_Market_Research_*.docx
Potential_Collaborations_and_New_and_Refine_Features.docx
